    "result_text": "All green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe identity key was redesigned from a plaintext pipe-delimited string (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) to a **SHA-256 hex digest** over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, and duplicate detection now flows entirely through that single key.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.java`**\n- `key(telephone, email, lastName)` now returns the full 64-char lower-case hex SHA-256 over the three normalized components (telephone \u2192 E.164, email \u2192 lower-cased/trimmed, last name \u2192 Soundex).\n- `of(Owner)` now feeds the owner's stored last name (instead of `householdId`).\n- Added a self-contained American **`soundex(lastName)`** implementation (first letter + up to three digits, zero-padded to 4; H/W don't separate, vowels do) and a full-length lower-hex helper.\n- `householdIdFor(...)` is untouched \u2014 `householdId` is still computed, stored, and returned (it still drives membership scoring), it just no longer drives 409s.\n\n**`CheckIdentityUnique.java`** \u2014 Now a single rule: 409 only when the new owner's identity key equals a live owner's. The separate household-duplicate block (and the `sharesHousehold` bypass) is gone. Deleted owners are still skipped; the email-domain blocklist still runs first in `ValidateOwner`.\n\n**`PossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 Soft match now triggers when **soundex(lastName) + postcode match but the identity key differs** (previously: exact last name + postcode + different telephone). Since telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different phones now fall through 409 and are flagged as a soft match. Removed the now-obsolete `sharesHousehold` suppression method and its callers in `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, and `CheckIdempotencyKey`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated descriptions for `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, and `sharesHousehold` to match the new behavior.\n\n## Tests\nBoth acceptance tests pass \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (identityKey matches `[0-9a-f]{64}`) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical telephone/email/lastName \u2192 409) \u2014 and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
